, default-only effort behavior, saved-selection validation and preservation of session identity, transcript and in-flight turns.","Assess observable picker flows and whether UX artifacts are necessary; inspect any supplied artifacts and renderings where available.","Verify unit and integration coverage addresses recovery and selection regressions, and that mixed releases preserve existing contracts."],"dependsOn":["scope","vibe"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"visuals","title":"Generated sequence and interaction-boundary evidence","selectors":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/companions","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","document:line:99"],"concerns":["Read the sequence definition, all participant descriptions and linked generated companion; inspect its actual rendering where available and report any mandatory verification limitation.","Check participant responsibilities, alternate daemon and chat entry points, catalog exchange, process/session ownership, preflight rejection and prompt-dispatch ordering against the contracts and actual integration boundaries.","Check companion paths, generated content and source descriptions agree with the live and canonical LLD; assess whether additional relationship or UX artifacts are materially necessary."],"dependsOn":["vibe","chat"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Whole-artifact completeness and upstream consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all substantive assessments against the originating ISSUE and ensure no fix-intent requirement or acceptance obligation is missing.","Check cross-chunk contradictions in catalog authority, selection defaults, error contracts, ownership, resume behavior, lifecycle, compatibility and deployment ordering.","Check live document, canonical artifact, citations, diagrams and test mappings agree; consolidate demonstrated defects