bf6bd47b036-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-97adabf6bd47b036.json","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:715","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts:1023","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:326","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3221","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts:147","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json:43","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py:1456","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/workflow-runs/97adabf6bd47b036/design.story-wf-1794242207248-a8o0ow.jsonl"],"limitations":["The analysis evidence referenced by /citations/0 as s1:structural-map could not be located in the repository or persisted workflow/analyze files. The workflow log records completion of context.assemble but contains no bundle content. Current code corroborates the reported launch and picker defects, but the cited bundle’s contents and provenance could not be verified."],"advice":["Give c1 a retrievable bundle identifier or persisted evidence path.","Clarify that empty shared-interaction sections mean no parent-HLD or sibling contracts; existing catalog IPC and execution-adapter dependencies remain applicable and are described elsewhere.","Keep installed-protocol and execution-policy qualification as a prerequisite to implementation: the inspected protocol declares session-only model and effort mutation, while end-to-end runtime parity still requires the planned qualification."]},{"chunkId":"vibe","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The installed Vibe implementation supports the selected session-only approach, including model aliases, effort mutation and runtime read-back. Catalog authority and local CLI authentication remain intact. The daemon retry integration needs an explicit contract to prevent replay after uncertain dispatch.","findings":[{"id":"vibe-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0/errors","message":"The design requires distinguishing pre-dispatch refusal from failure after dispatch and never replaying an uncertain prompt, but its error contract exposes only selection-unavailable and launch-failed, without dispatch certainty or a non-retryable marker. This matters at the existing daemon boundary: complete() and runEditSession() use withTransientRetry(), and runReviewSession() also retries failures based on error text. Reporting a post-dispatch connection failure through the existing caller-specific failure path can therefore launch another session and submit the prompt again. Specify the dispatch-state/error representation, the retry guards in these callers, and regression coverage for a lost turn/start response and a transient failure after accepted dispatch.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/0",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/errorPaths/errorCases/2",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/testStrategy","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:309 — withTransientRetry classifies errors by transienceText","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:504 — runEditSession uses withTransientRetry","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:570 — review-session retry handling","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:1049 — transienceText falls back to the error message"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts","vscode-plugin/tsconfig.json","vscode-plugin/esbuild.mjs","https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli","https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/configuration-reference","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_connection_protocol.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/config.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/server.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_unified_harness_backend_adapter.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/core/config/layers/environment.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/core/config/orchestrator.py"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make qualification fixtures explicitly cover daemon read-only tool filtering, headless approval denial, chat attachment roots, cancellation during preflight, deadline expiry, bounded event handling and the default-only fallback.","Record the qualified Vibe version and capability-detection mechanism. The installed initialize response exposes server identity and process ID, so method availability should not be assumed from an advertised method list.","Define the shared request/result/transport types and their module location, including caller-specific event and process-lifecycle mappings, before implementation."]},{"chunkId":"chat","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned sections and the catalog citation were inspected against the originating ISSUE and current chat implementation. The design captures the intended behavior, but leaves provider-aware reconciliation and the extension/webview recovery integration insufficiently specified.","findings":[{"id":"chat-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/signature","message":"reconcileRunConfig(next: RunConfig, catalog: RunCatalog) lacks the provider needed to select the applicable model list. The existing RunConfig contains only model and effort; provider belongs to ChatSession, while the catalog projection contains multiple providers. The parameter description incorrectly says RunConfig includes provider. Define a provider-aware input or explicit provider argument and the catalog type, retaining the existing persisted shape. Apply the same reconciliation to new-chat, set-run-config and restored selections so provider switches cannot carry an incompatible effort.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/1","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:294 — RunConfig contains only optional model and effort","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:110 — ChatSession owns provider","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:110 — runCatalogView produces per-provider model lists","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2501 — provider switching carries the previous effort","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3190 — new-chat and set-run-config mutation paths"]},{"id":"chat-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions","message":"The recovery contract requires reconnect and picker-open retries, loading/unavailable states and stale-response protection, but does not define the integration that delivers them. The current IpcClient has no reconnect subscription, the host receives only a definitions callback, and picker opening occurs entirely inside the webview without notifying the host. Catalog results currently replace the entire HTML document. Specify the reconnect observation mechanism, picker-open intent, catalog/status delivery and ready-handshake behavior, plus refresh-generation ownership across disposal/reopen. Define how updates preserve the active view and in-flight turn, and add an integration test that drives the actual picker/host boundary through initial failure and recovery; the listed host unit tests alone do not establish this path.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/testStrategy","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149 — IpcClient exposes request methods and optional streams, without reconnect notifications","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:880 — chat receives only the definitions request callback","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:327 — successful catalog loading calls setHtml(renderShell())","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2454 — catalog is parsed once at webview bootstrap","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2507 — picker opening does not notify the host","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3513 — webview reload requires the ready handshake","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:109 — run-config carries selection but no catalog/status","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1965 — existing picker wiring coverage checks generated script text"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:806","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:880","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:110","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:294","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/webview-channel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/models/definitions.ts","vscode-plugin/src/surfaces/status-surface.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1734","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1947","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5824","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5880","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:8240"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Specify the outcome when a successful catalog refresh finds a saved model missing or rejected, including what is persisted and communicated to the user.","Expand lifecycle test cases to name concurrent refresh coalescing, reconnect during an outstanding request, late responses after disposal/reopen, last-valid retention, empty effort lists and preservation of an already-dispatched turn's selection.","The existing picker layout can support this change without a separate UX mock. Document the loading/unavailable labels and remove the current Vibe note that describes effort as informational."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected. The generated companion preserves the canonical participants, messages and descriptions, and agrees with the LLD’s catalog exchange, alternate callers, session ownership and pre-dispatch verification contract. No demonstrated defect was found in this assignment. Actual visual verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/companions","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","document:line:99","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:715","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts:1023","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:326","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:880","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts:147","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py:1456","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py:2741","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/catalog-model-effort-lld-97adabf6.json"],"limitations":["The generated sequence-diagram.html source and descriptive tables were inspected, but its actual rendering could not be verified: opening the companion through the browser tool returned “The browser access host is unavailable.” Layout, clipping and runtime Mermaid rendering therefore remain unverified."],"advice":["Consider visually distinguishing the alternate chat/daemon entry points and the rejection/success branches. The current Mermaid sequence is linear; its accompanying descriptions correctly explain that the callers are alternatives and rejection prevents prompt dispatch.","The documented ownership and cardinality are sufficiently simple for the existing prose and sequence artifact; an additional ERD is unnecessary. The existing picker layout also does not require a separate UX mock solely for this change."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"All four completed substantive assessments were reconciled against the originating ISSUE and unchanged live/canonical LLD. The design covers the reported symptoms and fix intent; no additional distinct defect was demonstrated. Existing findings vibe-001, chat-001 and chat-002 remain blocking. Citation provenance and actual diagram rendering remain unverified, so the overall assessment is incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/catalog-model-effort-lld-97adabf6.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-97adabf6bd47b036.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:309","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:110","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:294","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts:1023","vscode-plugin/esbuild.mjs","Checkpoint completedChunks: scope, vibe, chat, visuals; live and canonical SHA-256 fingerprints match the attempt baseline."],"limitations":["The scope assessment could not locate the structural-map bundle cited as s1:structural-map. Its contents and provenance remain unverified; current code corroboration does not verify that citation.","The visuals assessment reported that browser access was unavailable. Companion source and descriptive tables agree with the canonical definition, but actual Mermaid rendering, layout and clipping remain unverified."],"advice":["Resolve vibe-001 by defining dispatch certainty and guarding every daemon retry boundary; cover lost turn/start responses and failures after dispatch.","Resolve chat-001 and chat-002 together: retain persisted configuration compatibility while defining provider-aware reconciliation and the host/webview refresh, status and lifecycle contracts.","Replace or explain ac1/ac2/ac3 in the acceptance mapping: the originating ISSUE contains prose fix intent rather than numbered acceptance criteria. The listed tests otherwise map to its execution, recovery and unsupported-selection obligations.","Retain protocol and policy qualification before deployment. The documented default-only fallback, unchanged catalog RPC and absence of data migration are consistent across sections.","Provide a retrievable structural-map citation and complete visual inspection before closing the review."]}],"limitations":["The analysis evidence referenced by /citations/0 as s1:structural-map could not be located in the repository or persisted workflow/analyze files. The workflow log records completion of context.assemble but contains no bundle content. Current code corroborates the reported launch and picker defects, but the cited bundle’s contents and provenance could not be verified.","The generated sequence-diagram.html source and descriptive tables were inspected, but its actual rendering could not be verified: opening the companion through the browser tool returned “The browser access host is unavailable.” Layout, clipping and runtime Mermaid rendering therefore remain unverified.","The scope assessment could not locate the structural-map bundle cited as s1:structural-map. Its contents and provenance remain unverified; current code corroboration does not verify that citation.","The visuals assessment reported that browser access was unavailable. Companion source and descriptive tables agree with the canonical definition, but actual Mermaid rendering, layout and clipping remain unverified."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"67346643855c882010518f215c6f5d5bf9a48133ba66514151dcc83c2ec37cbf"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T16:53:00.041Z"},{"number":2,"status":"incomplete","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"d8fc860320e4d29e6c3c4906e361425d93de7e197121993b678b5310172d9df9","document":"7f9b1f49ea6c88955be6fda229ca68879bac58f1eb143f69532d4ec160ad7823"},"contentIdentity":"dacbf2c6efe5402e20033b2eacdf8fe19d082a245e8658ab967b066adc139ea1","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794243289902-n9uk4z\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T16:54:51.247Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T16:34:12.401Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 1055,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"97adabf6bd47b036\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794243289902-n9uk4z\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"7f749d207e62c464e81117b192c65900c7061d416601d5ca3031a0b2a49c398f\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Apply catalog model and effort choices in daemon and VS Code\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 2\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Apply catalog model and effort choices in daemon and VS Code\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"prose\": \"Apply catalog-backed selections at the Vibe session boundary and recover the VS Code chat picker when the daemon catalog becomes available.\",\n      \"audience\": \"technical\"\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Vibe session launch\",\n          \"signature\": \"runVibeSession(request: VibeRunRequest, transport: VibeSessionTransport): Promise<VibeRunResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"request\",\n              \"type\": \"VibeRunRequest\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing prompt, working directory, permissions, attachments, native session, optional model and effort, and cancellation.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"transport\",\n              \"type\": \"VibeSessionTransport\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Caller-owned local process adapter for the installed Vibe app-server binary.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<VibeRunResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Verified effective selection, native session identity, and the same bounded events and outcome each caller consumes.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"selection-unavailable\",\n              \"condition\": \"Local protocol lacks a required capability, a catalog model cannot be mapped to an unambiguous allowed alias, or the runtime does not confirm the requested choice.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"launch-failed\",\n              \"condition\": \"Process startup, authentication, protocol, timeout, or tool-scope parity fails.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"dispatch-uncertain\",\n              \"condition\": \"Writing turn/start may have delivered bytes but no authoritative reply was received. This failure carries dispatchState: 'possibly-sent'.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"turn-failed\",\n              \"condition\": \"Vibe acknowledged turn/start before the failure. This failure carries dispatchState: 'accepted'.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Catalog models and effort levels remain sourced from models.definitions and the daemon registry. Discovery is limited to the local Vibe session and never grants access to a model absent from the catalog.\",\n            \"Explicit choices use the app-server path. Default-only invocations retain the existing headless behavior. Preserve the caller's existing working directory, tool approvals, attachment access, budgets, and abort signal.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Use one local process and at most one Vibe session per invocation. Start a new session or resume the supplied native ID without sending the prompt. Resolve catalog ID and aliases against the session's model choices, apply config/model/write with session_only true, and verify runtime model and effort before turn/start. A default model with explicit effort uses the verified effective model and its catalog levels.\",\n            \"Model aliases are accepted only when they resolve to the intended catalog ID. A returned failure, policy rejection, or mismatched effective selection stops before prompt delivery. Existing CLI credentials and configuration files are preserved.\",\n            \"Translate bounded native events into current daemon and VS Code outputs, including text, reasoning, tool activity and session identity. Preserve resume identity. Cancel or time out the owned turn and child, and distinguish failure after dispatch from a safe pre-dispatch refusal. Never replay an uncertain prompt.\",\n            \"Use a typed VibeSessionError with dispatchState 'not-sent' | 'possibly-sent' | 'accepted'. Enter possibly-sent before handing turn/start to the transport, including write and cancellation races. Enter accepted on a successful acknowledgement or authoritative turn event. Only a proven pre-dispatch failure can enter the existing transient retry path. The daemon complete() and runEditSession() retries and the separate runReviewSession() retry loop must consult this field before classifying error text. The chat adapter releases its turn lease and preserves its transcript and native session without automatic replay. A lost acknowledgement never resets the state.\",\n            \"Follow the installed stdio handshake in order. Send initialize, wait for the response, send initialized, open or resume, apply session-only config, then read runtime/read. The local probe confirmed a session-only high effort on an isolated loopback fixture, with no prompt and no config rewrite.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Chat catalog refresh and selection\",\n          \"signature\": \"refreshRunCatalog(): Promise<void>; reconcileRunConfig(provider: Provider, next: RunConfig, catalog: RunCatalog): RunConfig\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"provider\",\n              \"type\": \"Provider\",\n              \"purpose\": \"The target session's provider selects the model list from the catalog projection.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"next\",\n              \"type\": \"RunConfig\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing optional model and effort fields. Keep their persisted format.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"catalog\",\n              \"type\": \"RunCatalog\",\n              \"purpose\": \"In-memory projection keyed by provider, containing the existing per-provider model and per-model effort views.\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"RunConfig\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A selection whose effort is supported by the selected model, or its default effort.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"catalog-unavailable\",\n              \"condition\": \"The daemon is disconnected or fails its catalog request.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Provider discovery remains based on locally available chat adapters. Daemon tier settings retain their existing config gateway and model validation.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Coalesce concurrent catalog refreshes. Retry after reconnect or reopening the picker. Preserve the last valid catalog during transient failures and display a loading or unavailable state when there is no catalog. Ignore late or disposed responses.\",\n            \"Commit model and effort together. Retain the old effort only when the selected catalog model allows it. Show default as the only effort until a specific model is known. Preserve existing persisted chat selection until a valid catalog can evaluate it, and keep session identity, transcript, and in-flight turns intact.\",\n            \"Use provider-aware reconciliation for new-chat, set-run-config, and session restore. Persist provider and reconciled fields in one session update. Validate again on the authoritative host before a turn. Without catalog evidence, preserve restored choices but disable edits that depend on unavailable definitions.\",\n            \"The extension supplies its existing IpcClient reachability probe to the chat host. After a catalog failure, the host runs one bounded reachability probe per minute while a panel is open, without invoking an agent. A reachable daemon permits a coalesced catalog retry. The picker-open webview intent requests immediate refresh; a failing definitions request while the daemon is reachable remains retryable. Stop the timer on catalog success or panel disposal.\",\n            \"Keep cache, single-flight refresh, and monotonic generation on the chat host. Dispose or replace the webview binding before accepting another ready handshake. Ignore results from invalidated generations. Send a run-catalog snapshot with status, revision and provider projection on ready and after changes. The webview applies it to the picker state only and rerenders the open controls in place. Selection, transcript and active turn state stay on their existing channels.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"VibeRunRequest and effective selection\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Transient one-to-one ownership from a daemon run or VS Code turn to an owned Vibe process and session. A resumed session is referenced by its existing native ID. The returned model and effort confirm the request before dispatch. Credentials and existing saved settings stay in Vibe.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"VS Code chat run configuration\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"One session retains a provider, optional catalog model and optional supported effort. Many sessions can read the same in-memory catalog projection. Existing persisted fields and wire messages remain compatible.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts\",\n          \"vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"interactionWithShared\": [],\n    \"errorPaths\": {\n      \"errorCases\": [\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Catalog fetch fails or the daemon reconnects during a fetch\",\n          \"detection\": \"Read rejects, times out, or returns for an obsolete refresh generation.\",\n          \"response\": \"Keep the last valid catalog if present, expose unavailable state otherwise, and retry on reconnect or picker open.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"Model choices return without reopening the chat.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Vibe lacks a required method or cannot apply the selected model or effort\",\n          \"detection\": \"Capability negotiation, a negative mutation response, or read-back differs from the requested selection.\",\n          \"response\": \"Stop before submitting the prompt and surface a concise error that names the unsupported choice. Do not use an implicit default for an explicit selection.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The user can choose an available value or clear the override without losing the chat.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"scenario\": \"Vibe loses the turn/start acknowledgement or fails after dispatch\",\n          \"detection\": \"Transport closes, terminal event reports failure, or the owned deadline expires.\",\n          \"response\": \"Preserve dispatch certainty in the typed error and bypass all automatic transient retries when dispatch may have occurred. Release the child and preserve received output and session identity.\",\n          \"userImpact\": \"The user can inspect partial output and decide whether to retry.\",\n          \"recoverable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"edgeCases\": [\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Model changes from a high-effort choice to a model offering no effort choices\",\n          \"expected\": \"Persist the new model with default effort in one update.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"A saved model and effort are restored while the catalog is unavailable\",\n          \"expected\": \"Preserve the saved selection and defer validation until a successful refresh.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"No explicit model or effort was chosen\",\n          \"expected\": \"Preserve the existing headless defaults and output path.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"input\": \"Existing Vibe session resumes with a supported selection different from its prior settings\",\n          \"expected\": \"Confirm the selection in that session before starting its next turn. Preserve native session identity and caller policy.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"invariantsToPreserve\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Daemon tiers and VS Code read model and effort definitions from the existing catalog projection.\",\n          \"source\": \"c1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Existing run paths retain their prompt, provider authentication, policy, session resume, and cancellation behavior.\",\n          \"source\": \"c7\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"testStrategy\": {\n      \"testLevels\": [\n        {\n          \"level\": \"unit\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Protect catalog lifecycle and model-specific selection.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Chat recovers from a failed catalog request without losing session state\",\n            \"Chat validates effort on model switch and session restore\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Qualify both existing execution entry points with a fake Vibe process and verify preflight, output and cleanup.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Daemon and chat apply verified Vibe model and effort to new and resumed turns\",\n            \"Vibe preflight failures never submit or replay the prompt\",\n            \"Vibe protocol path preserves caller permissions, attachments, and terminal output\",\n            \"Lost turn/start acknowledgement and post-acknowledgement transient errors each dispatch once across daemon complete, edit and review retries\",\n            \"Real picker intent and ready handshake recover from initial catalog failure and reconnect without replacing the view or interrupting the turn\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"Scripted local app-server protocol fixture with capability, configuration, event, and cancellation cases.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"smoke\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Check the installed CLI contract using an isolated session with no cloud prompt.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Installed Vibe confirms a session-only model and effort without changing saved configuration\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"acceptanceMapping\": [\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac1\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Daemon and chat apply verified Vibe model and effort to new and resumed turns\",\n            \"Installed Vibe confirms a session-only model and effort without changing saved configuration\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac2\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Chat recovers from a failed catalog request without losing session state\",\n            \"Chat validates effort on model switch and session restore\",\n            \"Real picker intent and ready handshake recover from initial catalog failure and reconnect without replacing the view or interrupting the turn\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"criterionId\": \"ac3\",\n          \"provingTests\": [\n            \"Vibe preflight failures never submit or replay the prompt\",\n            \"Vibe protocol path preserves caller permissions, attachments, and terminal output\",\n            \"Lost turn/start acknowledgement and post-acknowledgement transient errors each dispatch once across daemon complete, edit and review retries\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"testFramework\": \"Node test runner with tsx, injected fake child process and chat panel fixtures. The standalone issue states acceptance in prose. The local mapping uses ac1 for effective execution selection, ac2 for picker recovery and compatible selection, and ac3 for safe dispatch and explicit failure.\"\n    },\n    \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"The daemon registry serves the catalog. Both Vibe launch paths omit effort, and the VS Code chat fetches its catalog once and stores model and effort independently.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"The same catalog drives validated choices. Explicit Vibe selections use verified session-only settings, and a chat can recover its catalog after a daemon reconnect.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Qualify the local Vibe protocol and execution policy parity. Deploy the daemon and VS Code builds with shared selection handling and typed preflight failures.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Reload the VS Code extension and restart the daemon through normal release operations when the build is installed. Retain existing model tier and chat records.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"Existing catalog RPC and saved config shapes remain valid. Older Vibe builds retain the default headless path and report unsupported explicit choices if session-only settings cannot be verified. A mixed daemon and extension release uses the same existing catalog wire shape. Rollback restores the prior selection behavior without migrating data.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": false\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Session-only Vibe settings\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Verify explicit overrides before dispatch.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Apply and verify local session settings while preserving existing default behavior.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Session-scoped changes and read-back\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Requires transport and policy parity\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Child environment configuration\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Apply child-local environment settings.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Keep headless invocation and express the selected model and thinking through a child environment.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Preserves headless transport\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Sparse effort overrides and resume precedence cannot be verified\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"S\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"The sparse environment route cannot reliably preserve complete model settings or precedence on resume.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"sequenceDefinition\": {\n      \"id\": \"catalog-model-selection\",\n      \"narrative\": \"The two execution callers apply and verify a Vibe session override before dispatching a prompt. The chat picker refreshes the existing catalog and reconciles the selected effort.\",\n      \"participants\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"chat\",\n          \"label\": \"VS Code chat host\",\n          \"description\": \"Owns picker state and sends a validated run selection.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"daemon\",\n          \"label\": \"Daemon and model catalog\",\n          \"description\": \"Serves the catalog and resolves the daemon's selected tier.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"adapter\",\n          \"label\": \"Local Vibe session adapter\",\n          \"description\": \"Owns a local child and gates prompt dispatch on verified settings.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"vibe\",\n          \"label\": \"Installed Vibe app server\",\n          \"description\": \"Opens or resumes a session and applies local session-only settings.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"from\": \"chat\",\n          \"to\": \"daemon\",\n          \"label\": \"Read models.definitions\",\n          \"description\": \"A picker-open intent or recovered daemon reachability asks the host to refresh its catalog.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"daemon\",\n          \"to\": \"chat\",\n          \"label\": \"Catalog or recoverable error\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"Publish the new catalog and status in place after the ready handshake, preserving the current chat and any last valid catalog.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"chat\",\n          \"to\": \"adapter\",\n          \"label\": \"Start selected chat turn\",\n          \"description\": \"Pass the model, allowed effort, resume identity and existing execution policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"daemon\",\n          \"to\": \"adapter\",\n          \"label\": \"Start selected daemon run\",\n          \"description\": \"The alternate caller passes the resolved tier and its existing run policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"adapter\",\n          \"to\": \"vibe\",\n          \"label\": \"Open or resume without a prompt\",\n          \"description\": \"Negotiate capabilities and obtain the local session identity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"adapter\",\n          \"to\": \"vibe\",\n          \"label\": \"Apply and verify session-only model and effort\",\n          \"description\": \"Resolve the catalog alias and verify the active model and effort before any turn.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"vibe\",\n          \"to\": \"adapter\",\n          \"label\": \"Effective selection or rejection\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"A rejection stops the adapter before it sends the prompt.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"adapter\",\n          \"to\": \"vibe\",\n          \"label\": \"Start turn once\",\n          \"description\": \"Dispatch only after effective values match and existing execution policy is applied.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"vibe\",\n          \"to\": \"adapter\",\n          \"label\": \"Bounded events and terminal outcome\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\",\n          \"description\": \"Preserve caller outputs and cancellation. Never replay a turn whose dispatch may have occurred.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"companions\": [\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/sequence-diagram.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Sequence diagram\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/model-definitions.ts:147\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"doc\",\n      \"ref\": \"https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/configuration-reference\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:309\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:326\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1 -->\n\n# LLD: STORY-97adabf6bd47b036-s1 — Apply catalog model and effort choices in daemon and VS Code\n\n## Summary\n\n**Epic:** `apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon`\n**HLD base run:** `wf-1794243289902-n9uk4z`\n**HLD effective hash:** `7f749d207e62...`\n\nApply catalog-backed selections at the Vibe session boundary and recover the VS Code chat picker when the daemon catalog becomes available.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [HLD context](#1-hld-context)\n2. [Contract details](#2-contract-details)\n3. [Data model changes](#3-data-model-changes)\n4. [Diagrams](#4-diagrams)\n5. [Error paths](#5-error-paths)\n6. [Test strategy](#6-test-strategy)\n7. [Migration](#7-migration)\n8. [Alternatives considered](#8-alternatives-considered)\n9. [References](#9-references)\n\n## 1. HLD context\n\n**Framework:** Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\n**Rollout phase:** standalone\n\n## 2. Contract details\n\n**Surface level:** internal-shared\n\n### 2.1 `Vibe session launch`\n\n```typescript\nrunVibeSession(request: VibeRunRequest, transport: VibeSessionTransport): Promise<VibeRunResult>\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `request: VibeRunRequest` — Existing prompt, working directory, permissions, attachments, native session, optional model and effort, and cancellation.\n- `transport: VibeSessionTransport` — Caller-owned local process adapter for the installed Vibe app-server binary.\n\n**Returns:** `Promise<VibeRunResult>` — Verified effective selection, native session identity, and the same bounded events and outcome each caller consumes.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `selection-unavailable` when Local protocol lacks a required capability, a catalog model cannot be mapped to an unambiguous allowed alias, or the runtime does not confirm the requested choice.\n- `launch-failed` when Process startup, authentication, protocol, timeout, or tool-scope parity fails.\n- `dispatch-uncertain` when Writing turn/start may have delivered bytes but no authoritative reply was received. This failure carries dispatchState: 'possibly-sent'.\n- `turn-failed` when Vibe acknowledged turn/start before the failure. This failure carries dispatchState: 'accepted'.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Catalog models and effort levels remain sourced from models.definitions and the daemon registry. Discovery is limited to the local Vibe session and never grants access to a model absent from the catalog.\n- Explicit choices use the app-server path. Default-only invocations retain the existing headless behavior. Preserve the caller's existing working directory, tool approvals, attachment access, budgets, and abort signal.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Use one local process and at most one Vibe session per invocation. Start a new session or resume the supplied native ID without sending the prompt. Resolve catalog ID and aliases against the session's model choices, apply config/model/write with session_only true, and verify runtime model and effort before turn/start. A default model with explicit effort uses the verified effective model and its catalog levels.\n- Model aliases are accepted only when they resolve to the intended catalog ID. A returned failure, policy rejection, or mismatched effective selection stops before prompt delivery. Existing CLI credentials and configuration files are preserved.\n- Translate bounded native events into current daemon and VS Code outputs, including text, reasoning, tool activity and session identity. Preserve resume identity. Cancel or time out the owned turn and child, and distinguish failure after dispatch from a safe pre-dispatch refusal. Never replay an uncertain prompt.\n- Use a typed VibeSessionError with dispatchState 'not-sent' | 'possibly-sent' | 'accepted'. Enter possibly-sent before handing turn/start to the transport, including write and cancellation races. Enter accepted on a successful acknowledgement or authoritative turn event. Only a proven pre-dispatch failure can enter the existing transient retry path. The daemon complete() and runEditSession() retries and the separate runReviewSession() retry loop must consult this field before classifying error text. The chat adapter releases its turn lease and preserves its transcript and native session without automatic replay. A lost acknowledgement never resets the state.\n- Follow the installed stdio handshake in order. Send initialize, wait for the response, send initialized, open or resume, apply session-only config, then read runtime/read. The local probe confirmed a session-only high effort on an isolated loopback fixture, with no prompt and no config rewrite.\n\n### 2.2 `Chat catalog refresh and selection`\n\n```typescript\nrefreshRunCatalog(): Promise<void>; reconcileRunConfig(provider: Provider, next: RunConfig, catalog: RunCatalog): RunConfig\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `provider: Provider` — The target session's provider selects the model list from the catalog projection.\n- `next: RunConfig` — Existing optional model and effort fields. Keep their persisted format.\n- `catalog: RunCatalog` — In-memory projection keyed by provider, containing the existing per-provider model and per-model effort views.\n\n**Returns:** `RunConfig` — A selection whose effort is supported by the selected model, or its default effort.\n\n**Errors:**\n- `catalog-unavailable` when The daemon is disconnected or fails its catalog request.\n\n**Preconditions:**\n- Provider discovery remains based on locally available chat adapters. Daemon tier settings retain their existing config gateway and model validation.\n\n**Postconditions:**\n- Coalesce concurrent catalog refreshes. Retry after reconnect or reopening the picker. Preserve the last valid catalog during transient failures and display a loading or unavailable state when there is no catalog. Ignore late or disposed responses.\n- Commit model and effort together. Retain the old effort only when the selected catalog model allows it. Show default as the only effort until a specific model is known. Preserve existing persisted chat selection until a valid catalog can evaluate it, and keep session identity, transcript, and in-flight turns intact.\n- Use provider-aware reconciliation for new-chat, set-run-config, and session restore. Persist provider and reconciled fields in one session update. Validate again on the authoritative host before a turn. Without catalog evidence, preserve restored choices but disable edits that depend on unavailable definitions.\n- The extension supplies its existing IpcClient reachability probe to the chat host. After a catalog failure, the host runs one bounded reachability probe per minute while a panel is open, without invoking an agent. A reachable daemon permits a coalesced catalog retry. The picker-open webview intent requests immediate refresh; a failing definitions request while the daemon is reachable remains retryable. Stop the timer on catalog success or panel disposal.\n- Keep cache, single-flight refresh, and monotonic generation on the chat host. Dispose or replace the webview binding before accepting another ready handshake. Ignore results from invalidated generations. Send a run-catalog snapshot with status, revision and provider projection on ready and after changes. The webview applies it to the picker state only and rerenders the open controls in place. Selection, transcript and active turn state stay on their existing channels.\n\n## 3. Data model changes\n\n### 3.1 `VibeRunRequest and effective selection` — new\n\nTransient one-to-one ownership from a daemon run or VS Code turn to an owned Vibe process and session. A resumed session is referenced by its existing native ID. The returned model and effort confirm the request before dispatch. Credentials and existing saved settings stay in Vibe.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts`\n\n### 3.2 `VS Code chat run configuration` — invariant-change\n\nOne session retains a provider, optional catalog model and optional supported effort. Many sessions can read the same in-memory catalog projection. Existing persisted fields and wire messages remain compatible.\n\n**Call sites:**\n- `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts`\n- `vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts`\n\n## 4. Diagrams\n\n- [Sequence diagram](docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/sequence-diagram.html)\n\n## 5. Error paths\n\n**Error cases**\n\n- **Catalog fetch fails or the daemon reconnects during a fetch** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Read rejects, times out, or returns for an obsolete refresh generation.\n  - Response: Keep the last valid catalog if present, expose unavailable state otherwise, and retry on reconnect or picker open.\n  - User impact: Model choices return without reopening the chat.\n- **Vibe lacks a required method or cannot apply the selected model or effort** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Capability negotiation, a negative mutation response, or read-back differs from the requested selection.\n  - Response: Stop before submitting the prompt and surface a concise error that names the unsupported choice. Do not use an implicit default for an explicit selection.\n  - User impact: The user can choose an available value or clear the override without losing the chat.\n- **Vibe loses the turn/start acknowledgement or fails after dispatch** (recoverable)\n  - Detection: Transport closes, terminal event reports failure, or the owned deadline expires.\n  - Response: Preserve dispatch certainty in the typed error and bypass all automatic transient retries when dispatch may have occurred. Release the child and preserve received output and session identity.\n  - User impact: The user can inspect partial output and decide whether to retry.\n\n**Edge cases**\n\n| Input | Expected |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Model changes from a high-effort choice to a model offering no effort choices | Persist the new model with default effort in one update. |\n| A saved model and effort are restored while the catalog is unavailable | Preserve the saved selection and defer validation until a successful refresh. |\n| No explicit model or effort was chosen | Preserve the existing headless defaults and output path. |\n| Existing Vibe session resumes with a supported selection different from its prior settings | Confirm the selection in that session before starting its next turn. Preserve native session identity and caller policy. |\n\n**Invariants to preserve**\n\n- Daemon tiers and VS Code read model and effort definitions from the existing catalog projection. [[c1]]\n- Existing run paths retain their prompt, provider authentication, policy, session resume, and cancellation behavior. [[c7]]\n\n## 6. Test strategy\n\n**Test framework:** `Node test runner with tsx, injected fake child process and chat panel fixtures. The standalone issue states acceptance in prose. The local mapping uses ac1 for effective execution selection, ac2 for picker recovery and compatible selection, and ac3 for safe dispatch and explicit failure.`\n\n**Test levels**\n\n- **unit** — Protect catalog lifecycle and model-specific selection.\n  - Subjects: `Chat recovers from a failed catalog request without losing session state`, `Chat validates effort on model switch and session restore`\n- **integration** — Qualify both existing execution entry points with a fake Vibe process and verify preflight, output and cleanup.\n  - Subjects: `Daemon and chat apply verified Vibe model and effort to new and resumed turns`, `Vibe preflight failures never submit or replay the prompt`, `Vibe protocol path preserves caller permissions, attachments, and terminal output`, `Lost turn/start acknowledgement and post-acknowledgement transient errors each dispatch once across daemon complete, edit and review retries`, `Real picker intent and ready handshake recover from initial catalog failure and reconnect without replacing the view or interrupting the turn`\n  - Fixtures: `Scripted local app-server protocol fixture with capability, configuration, event, and cancellation cases.`\n- **smoke** — Check the installed CLI contract using an isolated session with no cloud prompt.\n  - Subjects: `Installed Vibe confirms a session-only model and effort without changing saved configuration`\n\n**Acceptance mapping**\n\n| Criterion | Proving tests |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `ac1` | `Daemon and chat apply verified Vibe model and effort to new and resumed turns`, `Installed Vibe confirms a session-only model and effort without changing saved configuration` |\n| `ac2` | `Chat recovers from a failed catalog request without losing session state`, `Chat validates effort on model switch and session restore`, `Real picker intent and ready handshake recover from initial catalog failure and reconnect without replacing the view or interrupting the turn` |\n| `ac3` | `Vibe preflight failures never submit or replay the prompt`, `Vibe protocol path preserves caller permissions, attachments, and terminal output`, `Lost turn/start acknowledgement and post-acknowledgement transient errors each dispatch once across daemon complete, edit and review retries` |\n\n## 7. Migration\n\n**State before:** The daemon registry serves the catalog. Both Vibe launch paths omit effort, and the VS Code chat fetches its catalog once and stores model and effort independently.\n\n**State after:** The same catalog drives validated choices. Explicit Vibe selections use verified session-only settings, and a chat can recover its catalog after a daemon reconnect.\n\n**Zero downtime:** no — **Data rewrite:** no\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. Qualify the local Vibe protocol and execution policy parity. Deploy the daemon and VS Code builds with shared selection handling and typed preflight failures. — ↩ rollbackable\n2. Reload the VS Code extension and restart the daemon through normal release operations when the build is installed. Retain existing model tier and chat records. — ↩ rollbackable\n\n**Backward compat:** Existing catalog RPC and saved config shapes remain valid. Older Vibe builds retain the default headless path and report unsupported explicit choices if session-only settings cannot be verified. A mixed daemon and extension release uses the same existing catalog wire shape. Rollback restores the prior selection behavior without migrating data.\n\n## 8. Alternatives considered\n\n### 8.1 a1: Session-only Vibe settings — **CHOSEN**\n\nVerify explicit overrides before dispatch.\n\nApply and verify local session settings while preserving existing default behavior.\n\n### 8.2 a2: Child environment configuration\n\nApply child-local environment settings.\n\nKeep headless invocation and express the selected model and thinking through a child environment.\n\n**Rejected because:** The sparse environment route cannot reliably preserve complete model settings or precedence on resume.\n\n## 9. References\n\n- **[[c1]]** `code` `src/daemon/model-definitions.ts:147`\n- **[[c2]]** `prior-artifact` `docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md`\n- **[[c3]]** `code` `src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json`\n- **[[c4]]** `doc` `https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli`\n- **[[c5]]** `doc` `https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/configuration-reference`\n- **[[c6]]** `code` `/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py`\n- **[[c7]]** `code` `src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:309`\n- **[[c8]]** `code` `vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:326`\n- **[[c9]]** `code` `src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149`\n"},"capturedAt":"2026-11-09T16:55:09.501Z"},"inventory":{"units":[{"id":"/body/hldContextSlice","selector":"/body/hldContextSlice","title":"hldContextSlice","kind":"section"},{"id":"/body/summary","selector":"/body/sum