/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-97adabf6bd47b036.json","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:715","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts:1023","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:326","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3221","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts:147","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json:43","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py:1456","/Users/subhagho/.insrc/workflow-runs/97adabf6bd47b036/design.story-wf-1794242207248-a8o0ow.jsonl"],"limitations":["The analysis evidence referenced by /citations/0 as s1:structural-map could not be located in the repository or persisted workflow/analyze files. The workflow log records completion of context.assemble but contains no bundle content. Current code corroborates the reported launch and picker defects, but the cited bundle’s contents and provenance could not be verified."],"advice":["Give c1 a retrievable bundle identifier or persisted evidence path.","Clarify that empty shared-interaction sections mean no parent-HLD or sibling contracts; existing catalog IPC and execution-adapter dependencies remain applicable and are described elsewhere.","Keep installed-protocol and execution-policy qualification as a prerequisite to implementation: the inspected protocol declares session-only model and effort mutation, while end-to-end runtime parity still requires the planned qualification."]},{"chunkId":"vibe","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The installed Vibe implementation supports the selected session-only approach, including model aliases, effort mutation and runtime read-back. Catalog authority and local CLI authentication remain intact. The daemon retry integration needs an explicit contract to prevent replay after uncertain dispatch.","findings":[{"id":"vibe-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0/errors","message":"The design requires distinguishing pre-dispatch refusal from failure after dispatch and never replaying an uncertain prompt, but its error contract exposes only selection-unavailable and launch-failed, without dispatch certainty or a non-retryable marker. This matters at the existing daemon boundary: complete() and runEditSession() use withTransientRetry(), and runReviewSession() also retries failures based on error text. Reporting a post-dispatch connection failure through the existing caller-specific failure path can therefore launch another session and submit the prompt again. Specify the dispatch-state/error representation, the retry guards in these callers, and regression coverage for a lost turn/start response and a transient failure after accepted dispatch.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/0",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/errorPaths/errorCases/2",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/testStrategy","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:309 — withTransientRetry classifies errors by transienceText","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:504 — runEditSession uses withTransientRetry","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:570 — review-session retry handling","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:1049 — transienceText falls back to the error message"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts","vscode-plugin/tsconfig.json","vscode-plugin/esbuild.mjs","https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/work-with-cli","https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/cli/configuration-reference","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/protocol.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_connection_protocol.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/config.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/server.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/app_server/_unified_harness_backend_adapter.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/core/config/layers/environment.py","/Users/subhagho/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.14/site-packages/vibe/core/config/orchestrator.py"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make qualification fixtures explicitly cover daemon read-only tool filtering, headless approval denial, chat attachment roots, cancellation during preflight, deadline expiry, bounded event handling and the default-only fallback.","Record the qualified Vibe version and capability-detection mechanism. The installed initialize response exposes server identity and process ID, so method availability should not be assumed from an advertised method list.","Define the shared request/result/transport types and their module location, including caller-specific event and process-lifecycle mappings, before implementation."]},{"chunkId":"chat","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned sections and the catalog citation were inspected against the originating ISSUE and current chat implementation. The design captures the intended behavior, but leaves provider-aware reconciliation and the extension/webview recovery integration insufficiently specified.","findings":[{"id":"chat-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/signature","message":"reconcileRunConfig(next: RunConfig, catalog: RunCatalog) lacks the provider needed to select the applicable model list. The existing RunConfig contains only model and effort; provider belongs to ChatSession, while the catalog projection contains multiple providers. The parameter description incorrectly says RunConfig includes provider. Define a provider-aware input or explicit provider argument and the catalog type, retaining the existing persisted shape. Apply the same reconciliation to new-chat, set-run-config and restored selections so provider switches cannot carry an incompatible effort.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/1","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:294 — RunConfig contains only optional model and effort","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:110 — ChatSession owns provider","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:110 — runCatalogView produces per-provider model lists","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2501 — provider switching carries the previous effort","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3190 — new-chat and set-run-config mutation paths"]},{"id":"chat-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions","message":"The recovery contract requires reconnect and picker-open retries, loading/unavailable states and stale-response protection, but does not define the integration that delivers them. The current IpcClient has no reconnect subscription, the host receives only a definitions callback, and picker opening occurs entirely inside the webview without notifying the host. Catalog results currently replace the entire HTML document. Specify the reconnect observation mechanism, picker-open intent, catalog/status delivery and ready-handshake behavior, plus refresh-generation ownership across disposal/reopen. Define how updates preserve the active view and in-flight turn, and add an integration test that drives the actual picker/host boundary through initial failure and recovery; the listed host unit tests alone do not establish this path.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json#/body/testStrategy","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149 — IpcClient exposes request methods and optional streams, without reconnect notifications","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:880 — chat receives only the definitions request callback","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:327 — successful catalog loading calls setHtml(renderShell())","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2454 — catalog is parsed once at webview bootstrap","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:2507 — picker opening does not notify the host","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts:3513 — webview reload requires the ready handshake","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:109 — run-config carries selection but no catalog/status","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1965 — existing picker wiring coverage checks generated script text"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/2","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-97adabf6bd47b036-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/ISSUE.md","src/assets/models/cloud-model-catalog.json","src/daemon/model-definitions.ts","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:149","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:806","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:880","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:110","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts:294","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/webview-channel.ts","vscode-plugin/src/models/definitions.ts","vscode-plugin/src/surfaces/status-surface.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1734","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:1947","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5824","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:5880","vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts:8240"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Specify the outcome when a successful catalog refresh finds a saved model missing or rejected, including what is persisted and communicated to the user.","Expand lifecycle test cases to name concurrent refresh coalescing, reconnect during an outstanding request, late responses after disposal/reopen, last-valid retention, empty effort lists and preservation of an already-dispatched turn's selection.","The existing picker layout can support this change without a separate UX mock. Document the loading/unavailable labels and remove the current Vibe note that describes effort as informational."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected. The generated companion preserves the canonical participants, messages and descriptions, and agrees with the LLD’s catalog exchange, alternate callers, session ownership and pre-dispatch verification contract. No demonstrated defect was found in this assignment. Actual visual verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/companions","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","document:line:99","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/apply-catalog-model-effort-choices-daemon-E2026110997adabf6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/